WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:03.369
-Now, Kenan, you're always --
woop! --

00:00:03.369 --> 00:00:05.605
incredible
on "Saturday Night Live."

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:07.840
Rrp.
-♪ I appreciate it ♪

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:09.809
-Now, since a big part
of that show is

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:11.143
thinking fast, on the spot,

00:00:11.143 --> 00:00:12.946
I want to put your skills
to the test.

00:00:12.946 --> 00:00:15.214
It's time for "Think Fast!"

00:00:15.214 --> 00:00:17.316
♪ 1, 2, 3, Think Fast! ♪

00:00:17.316 --> 00:00:19.385
-We're gonna take turns
drawing one of these cards.

00:00:19.385 --> 00:00:21.621
Each card has five totally
random questions on it.

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:23.756
One person asks the questions,
the other person

00:00:23.756 --> 00:00:27.160
has to answer each question
as soon as it's asked.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.828
I mean, like, immediately.
Don't think.

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:30.797
Just go --
You basically --

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:32.498
-♪ 1, 2, 3, Think Fast! ♪

00:00:32.498 --> 00:00:35.134
-♪ You got to think fast
on your toes, yeah ♪

00:00:35.134 --> 00:00:36.369
-Yeah.
So, doesn't matter

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:38.337
if the answer is right or wrong,
just has to be

00:00:38.337 --> 00:00:39.972
the first thing
that pops into your head.

00:00:39.972 --> 00:00:43.643
Kenan, because you're the guest,
I will read the questions first.

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:45.077
-All right.
-You ready for this?

00:00:45.077 --> 00:00:47.046
Can we have
a little lighting change?

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:48.981
-Ooh.

00:00:48.981 --> 00:00:51.550
-What is a word
that doesn't rhyme with funk?

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:53.086
-Um, blam.

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:56.322
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:58.357
-What's sweeter than candy?

00:00:58.357 --> 00:00:59.726
-Sugar?

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:01.060
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:04.063
-If cats could play jazz,
what would it sound like?

00:01:04.063 --> 00:01:05.798
-♪ Meow meow meow meow meow ♪

00:01:05.798 --> 00:01:10.136
[ Meow scatting ]

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:11.304
Is that a question?

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:14.674
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.674 --> 00:01:16.609
-Why you got to be so rude?

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:17.944
-'Cause, man.

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:20.313
[Bleep]
I almost said a curse word.

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:21.747
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.747 --> 00:01:24.217
It's real out here.
It's real out here.

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:27.820
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:30.089
-That's my favorite one.

00:01:30.089 --> 00:01:32.325
Why do you deserve heartburn?

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:34.928
-Hey, you know, you got make
better choices, you know?

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:36.328
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.328 --> 00:01:37.796
Better choices.
-All right, here we go.

00:01:37.796 --> 00:01:39.732
Nice job on that, thinking fast.
Now, look...

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:41.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.836
That was some fast thinking.
Now it is my turn.

00:01:43.836 --> 00:01:46.038
Kenan, whenever you're ready,
take the card

00:01:46.038 --> 00:01:48.674
that's over by your section
and ask me the questions.

00:01:48.674 --> 00:01:50.977
Can we dim the lights, please?
[ Clears throat ]

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:52.778
-[ Laughing ]

00:01:52.778 --> 00:01:55.014
Why are ants so busy?

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:57.450
-Because they have to --
they feed their kids.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.185
-Yeah, man.
Yeah, they do.

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:01.154
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.154 --> 00:02:04.223
What's the worst podcast called?

00:02:04.223 --> 00:02:06.192
-"Showing Up
with Gill Gillerson."

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:07.693
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.693 --> 00:02:10.463
-All right.
What happened to the ducks?

00:02:10.463 --> 00:02:12.965
-They started a business
and it's --

00:02:12.965 --> 00:02:15.001
They're doing amazing overseas.

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:16.236
-That's good.
That's good.

00:02:16.236 --> 00:02:18.371
-Amazing, amazing stuff.
-It's a global world.

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:21.007
-Yeah, it really is.
-It's one world.

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:23.575
Why was Teddy
so angry at you on Tuesday?

00:02:23.575 --> 00:02:27.513
-Because of the party
that I didn't even know

00:02:27.513 --> 00:02:29.148
that was being thrown for Teddy.

00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:30.816
I was just there supporting.

00:02:30.816 --> 00:02:33.219
And I'm like, "Dude, I had
nothing to do with it."

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:36.422
And he's like,
"Save it, mister."

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:38.424
[ Laughter ]
-Wow. And Teddy's from...?

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:40.459
-Teddy's from --
He's from, actually, England.

00:02:40.459 --> 00:02:42.495
-Oh, got you.
-But he's an actor.

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:43.762
-Yeah, he tries -- yeah.
-He's an actor.

00:02:43.762 --> 00:02:45.264
He was in character.
-That's cool.

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:46.532
He does good voices.
I like Teddy.

00:02:46.532 --> 00:02:48.301
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:52.338
-What kind of man
microwaves his grapes?

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:53.773
-[ Voice breaking ] My --
My father.

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:55.574
-Oh, wow. This has gotten
really emotional.

00:02:55.574 --> 00:02:57.443
-My fa-- My father.
-Let's just take a moment.

00:02:57.443 --> 00:03:00.213
Let's, uh...
-I was swallowing my words.

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:02.715
My -- My father.
-Did he really do that?

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:06.252
-My dad.
My dad, his grapes --

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:07.887
-Did that disturb you
as a child?

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:10.556
-No, I'm fine talking about it.
-Okay.

00:03:10.556 --> 00:03:12.492
-Anyway,
my dad microwaves grapes.

00:03:12.492 --> 00:03:15.428
-That was chill, man.
That was a chill answer.

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:17.196
-It is time for the final round.
In this round,

00:03:17.196 --> 00:03:19.465
we'll both pick up a card with
the same set of questions.

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:23.202
We'll ask and answer them one at
a time, going back and forth.

00:03:23.202 --> 00:03:24.337
We'll go fast in this one.
Ready?

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:26.805
-Yeah. All right.
-All right?

00:03:26.805 --> 00:03:29.108
Here we go.
I will go first.

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:32.344
One, two --
Where do bagels come from?

00:03:32.344 --> 00:03:35.414
-The bread.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.414 --> 00:03:37.617
-The bread.
-What's your new nickname?

00:03:37.617 --> 00:03:40.119
-Uh, Scoopy G.
-Scoopy G.!

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:42.621
That's my dawg.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:42.621 --> 00:03:45.924
Why didn't we --
Why didn't we invite Erica?

00:03:45.924 --> 00:03:48.560
